@component local-bridge
@intent Detached WS bridge proxying a turn-based local IDE agent (Claude Code session) onto the live board. The real agent can't hold a WS socket in its tool loop (turn ends), so this resident process stands in: it holds the WS connection + HELLO, relays inbound (UserPrompt/Command/Cancel/AgentHello) into an **inbox file** the agent tails at safe points, and ships **outbox file** appends out as WS events (so the agent's progress shows on the board). On `AgentHello` (main role) it auto-replies a formal `OnboardAck` (welcome/guide/modes/policy) but **leaves Delegate to the main PM's judgment** (inbox-preserved, not auto-delegated). Scope = control/A2A bridge ONLY: it does NOT auto-capture the runtime's tool calls — TOOL_CALL/RUN events appear only if the agent explicitly mirrors them to the outbox (or uses a direct-WS adapter). Pure runtime, no DOM. (Distilled from dashboard/live/examples/ws-local-bridge.cjs — WS-PROTOCOL §13.9/§13.11.)
@expansion temperature=0.2 model=agent/claude template=estreux/v0.0.1
@targets vanilla
@profile protocol-adapter
@state
connected    : boolean = false   # WS open
backoff      : number = 500      # reconnect backoff ms (cap 8000)
seq          : number = 0        # outbound message sequence
runId        : string = null     # current run id (set by outbox {run:"start"})
outboxCursor : number = 0        # byte offset already shipped from outbox (init = EOF so pre-existing lines are skipped)
accepted     : boolean = false   # (v2.4.166 §13.25.13) first server frame that is neither SERVER_HELLO nor a server-emitted ConnectionRejected arrived — backoff resets here and nowhere earlier
admitted     : boolean = false   # (v2.4.166) the server's verdict is known: ConnectionInfo (sent only after every HELLO gate) or acceptance held ADMIT_HOLD_MS (3000) — online notice + outbox drain happen only here
refusedThisConn : boolean = false # server refused this connection — everything later on it is ignored (no inbox append, no auto-ack, no OnboardAck)
rejectedUntilRetry : number = 0  # >now = next attempt deferred to this instant (REJECT_RETRY_MS, default 5 min — not the backoff ladder)
streak       : object = null     # {code, since, count} — consecutive refusals with one code; one inbox line per streak; closed after acceptance held STREAK_HOLD_MS (10000)
@ports
in   wsUrl     : string          # ws://host:7878/ws (+ ?token= if set)
in   agentId   : string          # registration id (WS_AGENT_ID; main = main-agent; worker = own id)
in   agentName : string          # display name
in   threadId  : string          # channel/thread id (WS_THREAD_ID; default: main-agent→'local-ide', else AGENT_ID; worker must set its own to avoid showing as local-ide)
in   inbox     : string          # inbox file path the agent reads (WS_INBOX; worker = own queue)
in   outbox    : string          # outbox file path the agent appends to (WS_OUTBOX; worker = own queue)
out  inboxAppend(rec) : append routed inbound {at,name,value,source} to inbox file for the agent
deps ws        : websocket       # injected WS client (the bridge owns the socket the agent can't hold)
deps fs        : file IO         # inbox append + outbox tail (cursor-based)
deps token     : string          # optional LIVE_BOARD_WS_TOKEN
@behavior
connect          : open WS as agentId; handlers act only for their own socket (generation guard — a late event of an old socket never clears the new connection's state). On open send HELLO ({pid: process.pid, capabilities.inbound: UserPrompt/Command/Cancel/Priority}) only — **no backoff reset, no online notice** (v2.4.166: open is not acceptance; the Status auto-send stays disabled). ServerNotice(online) goes out on admission. Reconnect is scheduled from both error and close (Node 22/undici fires no close after error); a refused connection waits REJECT_RETRY_MS, a 4003/4403 close before admission with no refusal frame counts as a refusal, otherwise the backoff ladder (cap 8000).
onMessage(m)     : (v2.4.166 §13.25.13, before onInbound) server-emitted ConnectionRejected (source==='server' only — the server relays peer frames of any name) → refusedThisConn, accepted=admitted=false, discard held pre-verdict frames, noteRefusal: defer retry, console line per refusal, **one inbox line per streak** (first refusal / changed code / hourly re-alert, carrying `bridge.{retryInMs, streakSince, attempts}` and `targetAgentId` = own agentId so the turn-end probe surfaces it through its addressed branch) — the inbox is the agent's only channel, so it must learn, but not at the reconnect rate; then close the socket locally after 1.5 s if the server has not (otherwise a refused socket that stays open leaves the bridge deaf and mute with no reconnect scheduled). Anything else on a refused connection → ignored. First non-SERVER_HELLO frame → accepted (backoff=500, rejectedUntilRetry=0), arm admission hold + streak-close hold. Server ConnectionInfo → admitted. Before admission every frame is held (bounded 256) — no inbox append, no auto-ack/OnboardAck/UserPromptAccepted — and replayed through onInbound in order on admission.
send(type)       : (v2.4.166) refuses everything but HELLO until admitted — one gate at the socket edge instead of one per path.
refusalState     : (v2.4.166) retry deadline + streak persisted next to the lock (`.<agentId>-bridge.refusal`) and loaded at start; a start inside the deadline waits for it. A supervisor that respawns a bridge missing from the roster (a refused bridge always is) otherwise resets both on every roster change. The `pid` field enables the server-side §13.16.4 flap dampener to populate `incumbentPid` in the `ServerNotice{kind:'flap-rejected'}` payload with a real value rather than null — operator can identify which bridge instance is the incumbent during a churn event.
onInbound(m)     : SERVER_HELLO → log protocolVersion, return (not CUSTOM). ignore AgentList/History/CloseChannel (server→board). For other CUSTOM: append {at,name,value,source} to inbox. UserPrompt w/ promptId → send UserPromptAccepted(queued_for_next_safe_point). **AgentHello recognition broadened**: trigger auto-`OnboardAck` when `msg.name === 'AgentHello'` **OR** `msg.value?.type === 'AgentHello'` — the latter is the value-nested malformed shape a client may produce by misreading the `CUSTOM/AgentHello` slash shorthand. Accept it, but emit `console.warn('[bridge] AgentHello value-nested shape — client envelope mismatch; should use top-level name=AgentHello + top-level targetAgentId per Constellation.md §2')` (single line, silent-disable principle: acceptance broadened, mismatch surfaced). Then auto OnboardAck(targetAgentId=sender, contextId=msg.contextId||msg.threadId, parentId=msg.id, welcome/guide/modes(from state.json)/policy); Delegate NOT automated (left in inbox for main PM).
drainOutbox      : every 500ms tail outbox from cursor (reset if file shrank/replaced); ship each new line via emit. Holds (cursor unchanged) unless connected AND accepted AND admitted — draining before the verdict sends to a connection that may be refused and advances the cursor past lines it never delivered (v2.4.166; formerly pollOutbox).
emit(line)       : parse JSON (plain text → {say}). {say}→TEXT_MESSAGE_START/CONTENT/END · {run:"start"}→RUN_STARTED · {run:"finish"}→RUN_FINISHED · {step}→STEP_STARTED · {stepDone}→STEP_FINISHED · {tool}→TOOL_CALL_START · {type,...}→raw event.
gracefulExit(sig): on SIGINT/SIGTERM send ServerNotice(offline, "restart pending") — only if admitted (offline pairs with an online that was announced) — then close (flush ~300ms). SIGKILL can't run this → restarter should pre-announce ServerNotice(restarting).
@machine
# reducer: (connState, event) → connState
states: DISCONNECTED(initial) · CONNECTING · OPEN · ACCEPTED · ADMITTED · REFUSED
dispatch by event:
  start      : DISCONNECTED → CONNECTING   (entry: open WS)
  OPEN       : CONNECTING → OPEN           (entry: HELLO only; HELLO carries {agentId, pid: process.pid} for §13.16.4 incumbentPid)
  EVIDENCE   : OPEN → ACCEPTED             (first frame neither SERVER_HELLO nor server refusal; entry: backoff=500)
  VERDICT    : ACCEPTED → ADMITTED         (ConnectionInfo, or acceptance held 3 s; entry: ServerNotice online; outbox drains)
  REFUSAL    : OPEN|ACCEPTED|ADMITTED → REFUSED (server ConnectionRejected; entry: drop held frames, noteRefusal — one inbox line per streak, local close after 1.5 s if still open)
  CLOSE      : * → CONNECTING              (entry: REFUSED or refusal-coded close before ADMITTED → wait REJECT_RETRY_MS; else backoff, cap 8000)
derive:
  connected_gate ← emit() only ships when admitted (pre-verdict appends stay in the file; cursor inits at EOF)
  bridge_scope   ← control/A2A only; tool-call/run mirroring is the agent's explicit responsibility (no auto-capture)
@incident
bridge_pid (2026-06-01, main upstream Delegate seq 165, msgId m-mpua03au-164, ship trigger d385561): HELLO 봉투에 `pid: process.pid` 동봉 — 서버 측 §13.16.4 wsHelloFlapCheck 가 emit 하는 `ServerNotice{kind:'flap-rejected'}` 의 `incumbentPid` 가 현재 null (HELLO 에 pid 부재) → 실값으로 채워 churn event 중 incumbent 브릿지 식별 가능하게 함. Key 자체는 이미 존재(null 허용); 이번 패치는 값 공급. EG/bridge 후속 사이클.
